  "query_preview": "(Today through Friday)...\nIssued at 210 AM EDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nQuiet weather with above normal temperatures will continue through \nmuch of next week, with rain chances returning around Halloween.\n\nEarly This Morning through Sunday...\n\nSubsidence from upper ridging and surface high pressure will \ncontinue to provide dry conditions through Sunday. Winds will remain \nlight. High clouds will spill across the ridge into the area at \ntimes.\n\nLook for highs around 70 to the lower 70s today and in the lower to \nmiddle 70s Sunday. Lows will be in the 40s (did cut guidance for \nlows tonight in favored cold areas given what has happened recently).\n\nMonday through Wednesday...\n\nAn upper trough across southern Canada will help suppress the upper \nridge south on Monday, which will allow a surface cold front \nto sag into central Indiana on Monday. The front won't get much \nfarther south as upper flow will become near parallel to it. \nGenerally only high level moisture will be available, and upper \nsupport is nowhere nearby. Thus, dry conditions will persist.\n\nAdditional upper waves moving through the flow, mainly to the \nnorthwest of the area, will bring the front back north and out of \nthe area Tuesday into Wednesday. Again, little to no local forcing \nand no moisture will keep the area dry.\n\nHighs will be in the lower to middle 70s Monday and Wednesday. \nBehind the front on Tuesday, highs will be around 70 to the lower \n70s.\n\nThursday onward...\n\nWeak upper ridging will linger into Friday, keeping a front to the \nnorthwest and continuing the dry conditions with above normal \ntemperatures.\n\nUncertainty increases for Halloween as a broad upper trough begins \nto slowly approach the area. Some guidance has showers in the area \non Halloween while others keep them west until later Saturday night. \nWill stick with blended guidance's chance PoPs but with low \nconfidence. Temperatures look to remain above normal.",
